domain StructuredSemanticAuthoringKernelDesignV1Acceptance:
  description "Record exact owner acceptance of D11 implementation-design revision five without broadening execution authority."
problem P1:
  |
    Determine the lifecycle state and authority boundary after the owner received exact
    D11 design revision five following its corrected independent PASS review and
    instructed continuation.
evidence E_HISTORICAL_DESIGN:
  |
    Design Seal c4f8cb366d788d49a5769a7ec3cf2e31d97704a0c9eff17a4e23862330319394
    is the historical D11 implementation-design revision two accepted on 2026-09-11.
evidence E_HISTORICAL_REVIEW:
  |
    Historical review Seal d7144b116dec2b708cd8252ae4aea1d1078f3248123e86cd0c87734045aeee89
    reported PASS for exact revision two.
evidence E_HISTORICAL_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    On 2026-09-11, immediately after the revision-two re-review result was presented,
    the product owner replied ACCEPT. That acceptance completed the historical cb215
    design gate but did not authorize implementation or external effects.
premise HISTORICAL_ACCEPTANCE_INTERPRETATION:
  |
    The historical record originally interpreted the bundled ACCEPT as separate
    authority for eight provider calls, 500000 micro-USD per attempt, 240 seconds per
    attempt, 60 seconds per provider call, additive projection of owner-answer need onto
    the legacy failed status, source-reconstructed recovery, and progress thresholds.
evidence OWNER_AUTHORITY_CORRECTION:
  |
    On 2026-09-15, after the numerical limits and their effects were presented, the
    product owner stated that the limits were new information, identified time-based
    termination in particular as too strict, and instructed correction.
evidence E_ADR0032:
  |
    Accepted ADR0032 replaces unsupported provider-call and whole-attempt elapsed
    deadlines while preserving the non-time execution controls of ADR0031. It is the
    governing time-boundary correction for design revision five.
premise CORRECTED_POLICY_AUTHORITY:
  |
    The 2026-09-11 bundled ACCEPT is not authority to activate the rejected 60-second
    provider or 240-second whole-attempt semantics. Revision-five acceptance incorporates
    accepted ADR0032 and does not revive those historical values.
evidence E_DESIGN_REV5:
  |
    The exact received implementation-design revision five is Seal
    69c9c98937d7d610384823ae339ea464724f6e983d8b5500d3aef6942945a240
    and workfile SHA256
    426470047d0e380de90624192b9db71d3f30788fa44423ed0710f9cb1e6cdba4.
evidence E_REVIEW_REV5:
  |
    Corrected independent review Seal
    fc58bf3b2f9aaa9e6a0ac95ef21941c2523efc222aadec75c3bfa0626a44a1be
    reports PASS with no P0, P1, P2, or P3 findings. It does not require semantic-exact
    migration or an unaccepted formal materiality-proof protocol.
evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE_REV5:
  |
    On 2026-09-15, immediately after the corrected PASS result and correction scope were
    presented, the product owner instructed continuation and stated that the design is
    received. This binds acceptance to exact design revision five and its corrected
    review, not to a future revision or implementation result.
evidence OWNER_CONTINUATION:
  |
    The same 2026-09-15 instruction explicitly requested continuation. This is separate
    authority to resume the already selected local cc304 task after recording acceptance;
    it does not authorize paid provider calls, deployment, activation, or cc305.
premise BOUNDARY:
  |
    Acceptance establishes exact D11 implementation-design revision five and completes
    its current design gate. It does not by itself authorize implementation, provider
    calls, evaluation, deployment, production migration, candidate acceptance, pointer
    or policy activation, rollback, release, or successor-task start. OWNER_CONTINUATION
    authorizes only the separately bounded local cc304 continuation already selected in
    the accepted plan.
premise DOWNSTREAM_OBLIGATIONS:
  |
    Runtime F9 conformance, real create/revise/migrate route connection, authenticated
    answer and retry behavior, complete candidate reconciliation, controlled HTTP and UI
    evidence, provider quality evaluation, Stage proof, deployment, production migration,
    pointer changes, and final schema-three cutover remain at their named downstream
    gates. Design acceptance is not evidence that these outcomes are complete.
decision HISTORICAL_ACCEPTANCE based_on P1, E_HISTORICAL_DESIGN, E_HISTORICAL_REVIEW, E_HISTORICAL_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    Preserve D11 implementation-design revision two as the historical accepted snapshot
    and keep its review and acceptance evidence available in immutable history.
decision POLICY_AUTHORITY_CORRECTION based_on OWNER_AUTHORITY_CORRECTION, HISTORICAL_ACCEPTANCE_INTERPRETATION, E_ADR0032, CORRECTED_POLICY_AUTHORITY:
  |
    Preserve the prior authority correction. The rejected provider and whole-attempt
    elapsed deadlines are not reactivated by revision-five acceptance.
decision ACCEPTANCE_REV5 based_on P1, E_ADR0032, E_DESIGN_REV5, E_REVIEW_REV5, OWNER_ACCEPTANCE_REV5, BOUNDARY, DOWNSTREAM_OBLIGATIONS:
  |
    Accept exact D11 implementation-design revision five as the current reviewed design
    snapshot. This supersedes revision two only as the current design-acceptance target;
    it does not change the lifecycle status of ADR0031 or ADR0032 and does not claim
    implementation, provider, deployment, migration, activation, or release completion.
decision RESUME_CC304 based_on OWNER_CONTINUATION, ACCEPTANCE_REV5, BOUNDARY, DOWNSTREAM_OBLIGATIONS:
  |
    Resume only the already selected cc304 local implementation and verification task.
    Retain its existing exclusions and require separate authority for external effects
    and successor tasks.
evidence E_DESIGN_REV6:
  |
    The reviewed implementation-design revision-six Markdown SHA256 is
    a0f2ba909d3c71fb7de2235bd84125b420663f6f8b5400c4236eaf92e832ebff,
    and its authoritative reasoning SHA256 before acceptance is
    69eb577b09356a3806fd08325a9c73b78e6c864aa78e2947c489dff706b69f6d.
evidence E_ADR0033_REV1:
  |
    The reviewed ADR0033 revision-one authoritative SHA256 is
    ae8b736857b59188880acbf397e2da941caf5c102539b2410ddd7011fd1f529a.
evidence E_REVIEW_REV6:
  |
    Formal review reasoning SHA256
    cdd328284fd76310ef28dfaff0f59c2e7cf559828c738a3a71c85839be1567d3
    reports PASS with no P0 through P3 findings for ADR0033 revision one and design
    revision six.
evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE_REV6:
  |
    On 2026-09-15, immediately after the PASS result, complete Japanese review scope,
    and explicit statement that ACCEPT would receive both ADR0033 revision one and
    design revision six, the product owner replied "ACCEPT".
premise REV6_BOUNDARY:
  |
    Revision-six acceptance replaces revision five only as the current accepted design
    snapshot. It keeps exact provider timeout, worker lease, and bounded transport-
    recovery values undecided and does not authorize implementation, commit, push,
    provider calls, deployment, migration, activation, rollback, or release.
premise REV6_IMPLEMENTATION_OBLIGATION:
  |
    Implementation must retain a durable claim or expiry fact sufficient to decide
    worker-lease expiry after restart without requiring a durable Config identity or
    Config snapshot.
decision ACCEPTANCE_REV6 based_on E_DESIGN_REV6, E_ADR0033_REV1, E_REVIEW_REV6, OWNER_ACCEPTANCE_REV6, REV6_BOUNDARY, REV6_IMPLEMENTATION_OBLIGATION:
  |
    Accept exact implementation-design revision six as the current design snapshot in
    conformance with accepted ADR0033 revision one. Preserve revision five as immutable
    history and retain the stated authority boundary and implementation obligation.
